cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use LUMINA in any published work — including papers, preprints,
  theses, technical reports, blog posts, or derived software — please cite
  the associated manuscript. Citation is required by the CC BY-NC 4.0
  license under which this repository is distributed.
title: "LUMINA: Large Language Model Understanding Systematic Review & Meta-Analysis Integrated In Networked Agents"
abstract: >-
  An agentic LLM framework for title/abstract screening in systematic
  reviews and meta-analyses. Four cooperating agents (Classifier, PICOS
  Detailed Screener, Reviewer, Improver) operate through a bounded
  review/improve loop and produce a full written audit trail per
  inclusion decision. On 15 published SRMAs LUMINA achieves mean
  sensitivity 0.982 at specificity 0.879.
type: software
